	('553ba515-0040-433b-8220-c194f58dae2a', 'TVET Test 2 (Emotional)', 'Read the scenario and answer it according to your most likely reaction. There is a tendency to try to choose the âcorrectâ answer or what you think the test designer thinks is the correct answer. It is important to answer the questions honestly it you want an accurate appraisal of your emotional score.\n\nThere is no time limit for this test. \n', '[{"type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Upset. You assume your car could have any number of costly problems.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Concerned about your car, but still in a good mood overall you just make sure to call a mechanic first thing in the morning.","option_id":2,""is_correct":false},{""option":"You still feel good about your day, but know you will have to get your car looked at eventually.","option_id":3,""is_correct":false},{""option":"You decide to ignore your car completely, because you donât want to ruin your good mood.","option_id":4,""is_correct":false}],""question":"1.\tYou are leaving work for the weekend in a great mood. The work week went very well and you have some special plans this weekend that you are really looking forward to. As you leave work and get in your car, you notice that it wonât start. After a while you finally get it started, but now you feel: ","image_url":null,""slider_max":null,""slider_min":null,""is_required":false,""num_ratings":null,""question_id":1,""allow_recording":false,""media_file_type":"Image","slider_interval":1,""allow_multiple_files":false,""allow_multiple_selection":false},{""type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Tell the driver to calm down since it was only a minor accident and no one was hurt.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Explain to the driver that the fault rests with both of us and we should let the insurance companies figure it out.","option_id":2,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Patiently wait for the driver to calm down before you try to exchange information.","option_id":3,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Start yelling back at the driver, insisting that if itâs anyoneâs fault here itâs obviously his.","option_id":4,""is_correct":false}],""question":"You are driving in your car and get into a minor accident. No one is injured and there is only very minor damage to both vehicles. Itâs apparent that the accident was caused equally by both drivers. The other driver gets out of his car, and starts yelling, âYou idiot, look what youâve done to my car! This is your entire fault.â You: ","image_url":null,""slider_max":null,""slider_min":null,""is_required":false,""num_ratings":null,""question_id":2,""allow_recording":false,""media_file_type":"Image","slider_interval":1,""allow_multiple_files":false,""allow_multiple_selection":false},{""type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Decide to stay home, even though you wanted to go.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Go to the party but only talk with the people you already know.","option_id":2,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Talk mostly with your friends unless a stranger approaches your circle and starts conversing with you.","option_id":3,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Make an effort to meet new people and try to talk to people at the party who you donât know.","option_id":4,""is_correct":false}],""question":"A friend invites you to a party. Although you think a few friends of yours will be attending, you know that most of the people at the party are people whom you have never met before. You:","image_url":null,""slider_max":null,""slider_min":null,""is_required":false,""num_ratings":null,""question_id":3,""allow_recording":false,""media_file_type":"Image","slider_interval":1,""allow_multiple_files":false,""allow_multiple_selection":false},{""type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Meet them for lunch but promise yourself you will not let it go any further than that.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Decline the lunch invitation because you do not trust yourself with them.","option_id":2,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Meet them for lunch and let what happens happen. Your current partner doesnât ever need to know about it.","option_id":3,""is_correct":false}],""question":"You were in a serious relationship several years ago and were completely in love. Your partner broke off the relationship and you were crushed. He or she contacts you again years later and asks to meet for lunch. You still have feelings for the person, but you are in a relationship with someone else right now. You:","image_url":null,""slider_max":null,""slider_min":null,""is_required":false,""num_ratings":null,""question_id":4,""allow_recording":false,""media_file_type":"Image","slider_interval":1,""allow_multiple_files":false,""allow_multiple_selection":false},{""type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Tell them the relationship is no longer working and you want to break it off.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Tell them the relationship is in trouble and something needs to change.","option_id":2,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Try to change the relationship for the better without discussing it with your partner.","option_id":3,""is_correct":false}],""question":"You have been in a long-term relationship and the last few months have been stressful and routine. You are starting to get on each otherâs nerves and no longer feel any joy spending time with each other. You:","image_url":null,""slider_max":null,""slider_min":null,""is_required":false,""num_ratings":null,""question_id":5,""allow_recording":false,""media_file_type":"Image","slider_interval":1,""allow_multiple_files":false,""allow_multiple_selection":false},{""type":"Multiple Choice","comment":null,""options":[{""option":"Cancel the trip.","option_id":1,""is_correct":false},{""option":"Stand firm and leave for vacati